#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deployment with Portainer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get Zammad running is via a graphical docker UI. We "
"recommend [Portainer](https://www.portainer.io/). For installation "
"instructions, check out [Portainer's "
"documentation](https://docs.portainer.io/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Add Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the Portainer GUI (e.g. `https://yourdomain.tld:9443`), choose your "
"target environment, select **Stacks** and choose `Add stack` as you can see "
"in the screenshot below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Build From Repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Switch to **Repository** build method and provide the information below: - "
"**Name**: enter a desired name of the stack - **Repository URL**: "
"`https://github.com/zammad/zammad-docker-compose` - **Repository "
"reference**: `refs/heads/master` - **Compose path**: `docker-compose.yml` "
"(default)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Optional: if you need to provide environment variables, you can enter them "
"in the **Environment variable** section or even upload a .env file. See [env "
"template](https://github.com/zammad/zammad-docker-compose/blob/master/.env.dist)  "
"as an example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:47
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Deploy the Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:50
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:92
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After the stack is ready, you can access Zammad via the configured docker "
"host and port, e.g. `http://localhost:8080/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot in the Stacks section and highlighted \"Add "
"stack\".](/screenshots/installation/portainer-stacks.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Stack creation with provided information in Repository "
"screen](/screenshots/installation/portainer-stack-creation.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:55
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deployment with Docker-Compose"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Clone the GitHub Repo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "git clone https://github.com/zammad/zammad-docker-compose.git\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Make sure to run `git pull` frequently to fetch updates. Alternatively, you "
"can download the files from the [releases "
"page](https://github.com/zammad/zammad-docker-compose/releases)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Adjust Environment as Needed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:72
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In some cases our default environment is not what a docker-compose user is "
"looking for. See [Docker Environment "
"Variables](/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md) for details on which settings "
"can be configured."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:73
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to use a `.env` file, you can use the provided `.env.dist`\n"
"file and copy it to `.env`. That way it will be picked up by "
"Docker-Compose\n"
"automatically and not overwritten during updates.\n"
"\n"
"Zammad runs on port `8080` by default. If you want to use another port,\n"
"you can set it via the variable `NGINX_EXPOSE_PORT`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:82
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Start the Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:83
#: src/en/get-started/update.md:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "cd zammad-docker-compose\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker compose up -d\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:93
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Customizing the Zammad Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's necessary to apply local changes to the Zammad docker stack, "
"e.g. to include additional services. If you plan to do so, we recommend that "
"you do not change the `docker-compose.yml` file, but instead create a local "
"`docker-compose.override.yml` that includes all your modifications.  "
"Docker-Compose will [automatically load this file and merge its changes into "
"your stack](https://docs.docker.com/compose/multiple-compose-files/merge/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:102
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run Commands in the Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The docker entrypoint script sets up environment variables required by "
"Zammad to function properly. That is why calling `rails` or `rake` on the "
"console should be done via one of the following methods:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:109
#, markdown-text
msgid "Directly execute a specific command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver rails r '...your rails command "
"here...'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid "Run the interactive rails console to manually enter Rails commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver rails c\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:117
#, markdown-text
msgid "Via \"docker exec\":"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:117
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker exec zammad-docker-compose-zammad-railsserver-1 /docker-entrypoint.sh "
"rails r '...your rails command here...'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:121
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you need to retrieve information from the rails server, you can, for "
"example,\n"
"place `pp` (pretty print) in front of your rails command. This leads to an\n"
"output in your terminal.\n"
msgstr ""

