#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/console.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rails Console"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad uses Ruby on Rails so you can make use of the [rails "
"console](http://guides.rubyonrails.org/command_line.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please double check your commands before running, as some of those\n"
"commands might cause data loss or damaged tickets! If you're unsure,\n"
"**use a test system first**!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Starting Zammad's Rails Console"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute a Single Command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace `{COMMAND}` with your command you want to run.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you enter a `p` in front of your command (e.g. like\n"
"`rails r 'p Delayed::Job.count'`), you'll actually receive a printed\n"
"output (without you won't!).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs key:installmethod)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Docker Installation\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver rails r '{COMMAND}'\n"
"```\n"
"=== Package Installation\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"zammad run rails r '{COMMAND}'\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== Source / Development Installation\n"
"```sh\n"
"rails r '{COMMAND}'\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run Interactive Rails Console"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs key:installmethod)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Docker Installation\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver rails c\n"
"```\n"
"=== Package Installation\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"zammad run rails c\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== Source / Development Installation\n"
"```sh\n"
"rails c\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rails Console Safe Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Normally, starting rails console requires certain [third-party "
"services](/en/get-started/installation/prerequisites#server-software)  to be "
"up and running. You may receive errors and console will refuse to start in "
"case they are not available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:83
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"However, it's possible to start rails console in safe mode by setting a "
"special environment variable. With `ZAMMAD_SAFE_MODE=1` set, these checks be "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZAMMAD_SAFE_MODE=1 zammad run rails c\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:90
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Get the RAW Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The following command will help you to check on received EML-files Zammad "
"fetched. This comes in handy if you delete Mails upon fetching and you need "
"to check the EML-file itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To get the first articles EML-file, you can use the following command.  In "
"our example the ticket number in question is `101234`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.find_by(number:'101234').articles.first.as_raw.content\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If needed, you can also get the raw content of later articles (you'll need "
"to find the correct article though). Again, we expect `101234` to be our "
"ticket number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:109
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the first step we get all article IDs of the ticket:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.find_by(number:'101234').article_ids\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid "Output:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "[4, 3, 2]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:118
#, markdown-text
msgid "From the list we get, we can then get the articles content:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket::Article.find(3).as_raw.content\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you just use `Ticket::Article.find(3)` you can see further\n"
"information (like who sent the mail, when we fetched it, ...).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:127
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Update All Tickets of a Specific Customer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:129
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that this action can be expensive resource wise, if you\n"
"have many tickets, this might slow down Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.where(customer_id: 4).update_all(customer_id: 1)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:138
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Get Ticket State Types"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:141
#, markdown-text
msgid "This will show all state types needed for creating new ticket states:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket::StateType.pluck(:id, :name)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:147
#, markdown-text
msgid "Above will return both, the type ID and name - e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "`[[1, \"new\"], [2, \"open\"], ...`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:152
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:154
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:158
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In order to work on user information or to check for specific information, "
"you'll need to find it first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:160
#, markdown-text
msgid "User ID already known:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find(4)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:164
#, markdown-text
msgid "Searching for the user by his email address:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(email: 'your@email')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:168
#, markdown-text
msgid "Searching for the user by his login:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:168
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(login: 'john.doe')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:172
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unlock a Locked User Account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:174
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlocking a locked user account is also supported by Zammad's web UI!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:182
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It sometimes happens that a user locks himself out by wildly trying the\n"
"wrong password multiple times. Depending on your maximum failing login\n"
"count (<span class=\"title-ref\">default: 10 times</span>), Zammad might\n"
"lock the account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:185
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The user can't login any more (forever) if he doesn't change the password or "
"you reset the counter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "u=User.find(**USERID**)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.login_failed=0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:192 src/en/reference/console.md:219
#: src/en/reference/console.md:236 src/en/reference/console.md:253
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.save!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:199
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can also double check if the account is locked by running the following "
"command (result needs to be 1 above your limit, so 11 for the default of 10 "
"failing logins):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find(**USERID**).login_failed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:204
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change / Update Email Address of User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:207
#, markdown-text
msgid "If needed, you can simply change the email address of the user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:208
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that the login attribute is not affected by this and\n"
"Zammad thus might show different information within the UI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:213 src/en/reference/console.md:230
#, no-wrap
msgid "u = User.find(**USERID**)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:216
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.email = 'user@exmaple.com'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:224 src/en/reference/console.md:241
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need to find the user ID of the user first for this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:225
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change / Update Login Name of User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:229
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change the user name of the user (e.g. if you want to login with a shorter "
"username instead of a mail address)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.login = 'user@exmaple.com'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:242
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set Admin Rights for User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:246
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Don't have access to Zammad anymore? Grant yourself or another user "
"administrative rights."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "u = User.find_by(email: 'you@example.com')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.roles = Role.where(name: ['Agent', 'Admin'])\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:257
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set Password for User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:261
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You or the user did forget his password? No problem! Simply reset it by hand "
"if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:262
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"User.find_by(email: 'you@example.com').update!(password: "
"'your_new_password')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:266
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remove Password for User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:273
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you added a second authentication method (e.g. LDAP) after launch, there "
"still may be a password in Zammad's own user management. In cases like that "
"users will be able to login with their (local) Zammad password in addition "
"to the credentials stored on the external authentication provider. Simply "
"remove the password stored by Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:274
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(email: 'you@example.com').update!(password: nil)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:278
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Group Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:280
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find a Group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:282
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group.find_by(name: 'Users').follow_up_possible\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:286
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Chat Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:288
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remove IP Address Logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:292
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the following command to remove all IP address records from closed chats "
"that haven't been updated in the last seven days:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:293
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Chat::Session.where(state: 'closed').where('updated_at < ?', "
"7.days.ago).each do |session|\n"
"next if session.preferences['remote_ip'].blank?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:297
#, no-wrap
msgid "session.preferences.delete('geo_ip')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "session.preferences.delete('remote_ip')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:303
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"session.save!(touch: false)\n"
"end\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:308
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:312
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In this section, you can find some settings which you can set in the Zammad "
"UI as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:313
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Auto Shutdown Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:320
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Defines if an automatic shutdown of Zammad is performed when the the "
"database has been changed (e.g. after custom attributes have been created in "
"the object manager).  The underlying system (Systemd, Docker, Kubernetes) "
"will then restart the processes/containers after this shutdown. The default "
"setting is `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:323
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Setting this to ``false`` might only make sense in very rare cases and you "
"have to restart the Zammad services then manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:324
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('auto_shutdown', 'true')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:328
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket_hook Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:333
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This will give you the ticket hook that you'll find inside the `[]` in front "
"of the ticket number. By default this will be `Ticket#` - you shouldn't "
"change this setting in a productive system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ticket_hook')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:338
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "FQDN Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:341
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current FQDN setting of Zammad and, if needed, adjust it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:342
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This setting has no effect on SSL certificates or any web server\n"
"configurations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:348
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get current FQDN:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:348
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('fqdn')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:352
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set a new FQDN:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:352
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('fqdn', 'new.domain.tld')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:356
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP(s) Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:360
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This setting indirectly belongs to your FQDN setting and is relevant for "
"variable based URLs (e.g. in notifications) Zammad generated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:361
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This setting also affects Zammad's CSRF token behavior. If you set\n"
"this to e.g. HTTPs but you're using HTTP, logging in will\n"
"fail!\n"
"\n"
"It has no effect on SSL certificates or any web server configuration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:370
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current http type:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:370
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('http_type')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:374
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change the http type to HTTPs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:374
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('http_type', 'https')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:378
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Storage Provider Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:384
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The storage provider setting is set to `DB` on default installations.  "
"However, if you receive a lot of attachments or have a fairly busy "
"installation, using the database to store attachments is not the best "
"approach."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:386
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current attachment storage:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:386
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('storage_provider')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:390
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change attachment storage to database"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:390
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('storage_provider', 'DB')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:399
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have already stored files and want to move them, you can use the "
"following example. Please be aware that this operation should only be "
"executed in non-productive environments. In case you have to perform it in "
"production environments, you should specify a sleep delay - otherwise your "
"Zammad can be unresponsive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:401
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Move files from DB to File with a specified delay after each file in "
"seconds:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:402
#, no-wrap
msgid "Store::File.move('DB', 'File', delay_in_sec)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:407
#, markdown-text
msgid "The following settings are available in a default installation:"
msgstr ""

