#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:449
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('proxy', 'proxy.example.com:3128')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:452
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('proxy_username', 'some user')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:455
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('proxy_password', 'some pass')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:459
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hidden Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:464
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In this section you can find some settings that you won't find within the "
"Zammad UI. Those settings might come in handy as it can change Zammad's "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:465
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Send All Outgoing E-Mails to a BCC-Mailbox"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:471
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This option allows you to send all outgoing E-Mails (not notifications)  to "
"a specific mailbox. Please note that this shouldn't be a mailbox you're "
"importing already! This will apply to all groups and is a global setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:472
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('system_bcc', 'alias@domain.tld')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:477
#, markdown-text
msgid "You can easily check the current BCC-Setting by running the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:478
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('system_bcc')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:482
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate Counter on Grouped Overviews"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:485
#, markdown-text
msgid "This enables a ticket number value in each heading for grouped elements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:487
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enable counter for grouped overviews:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:487
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_table_group_by_show_count', true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:491
#, markdown-text
msgid "Disable counter for grouped overviews:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:491
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_table_group_by_show_count', false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:495
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get current setting (`nil` is false):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:495
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ui_table_group_by_show_count')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:499
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Default Ticket Type on Creation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:503
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad allows you to define the default article type upon ticket "
"creation. By default this will be a incoming phone call."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:505
#, markdown-text
msgid "You can choose between"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:509
#, markdown-text
msgid "`phone-in` (incoming call, **default**),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:509
#, markdown-text
msgid "`phone-out` (outgoing call) and"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:509
#, markdown-text
msgid "`email-out` (Sending an E-Mail out)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:510
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_ticket_create_default_type', 'email-out')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:515
#, markdown-text
msgid "To check what setting is set currently, simply run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:516
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ui_ticket_create_default_type')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:520
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding a Warning to the Ticket Creation Process"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:524
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to give your agent a note or warning during ticket **creation**, "
"you can do so with the below command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:526
#, markdown-text
msgid "You can use three different warnings for:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:530
#, markdown-text
msgid "Incoming Calls `:\"phone-in\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:530
#, markdown-text
msgid "Outgoing Calls `:\"phone-out\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:530
#, markdown-text
msgid "Outgoing E-Mails `:\"email-out\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:531
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setting.set('ui_ticket_create_notes', {\n"
"      :\"phone-in\"=>\"You're about to note a incoming phone call.\",\n"
"      :\"phone-out\"=>\"You're about to note an outgoing phone call.\",\n"
"      :\"email-out\"=>\"You're going to send out an E-Mail.\"\n"
"   })\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:539
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use those three sub-settings independently, if you e.g. don't\n"
"need a warning on incoming calls, simply leave out `:\"phone-in\"=>\"\"`\n"
"out of the setting. The setting itself is done within an array ( `{}` ).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:546 src/en/reference/console.md:586
#, markdown-text
msgid "To check what's currently set, you can use:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:547
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ui_ticket_create_notes')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:552
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding a Warning to the Article Reply Process"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:556
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to give your agent a warning during the ticket article "
"**reply**, you can do that with the command below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:559
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can provide different warnings for different channels and article "
"visibility:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:566
#, markdown-text
msgid "Internal Notes `:\"note-internal\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:566
#, markdown-text
msgid "Public Notes `:\"note-public\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:566
#, markdown-text
msgid "Internal Calls `:\"phone-internal\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:566
#, markdown-text
msgid "Public Calls `:\"phone-public\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:566
#, markdown-text
msgid "Internal Emails `:\"email-internal\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/console.md:566
#, markdown-text
msgid "Public Emails `:\"email-public\"=>\"\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:567
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setting.set('ui_ticket_add_article_hint', {\n"
"      :\"note-internal\"=>\"You are writing an |internal note|, only people "
"of your organization will see it.\",\n"
"      :\"note-public\"=>\"You are writing a |public note|.\",\n"
"      :\"phone-internal\" => \"You are writing an |internal phone note|, "
"only people of your organization will see it.\",\n"
"      :\"phone-public\"=>\"You are writing a |public phone note|.\",\n"
"      :\"email-internal\" => \"You are writing an |internal Email|, only "
"people of your organization will see it.\",\n"
"      :\"email-public\"=>\"You are writing a |public Email|.\"\n"
"   })\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:578
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use example sub-settings above independently, if you e.g.\n"
"don't need a warning on internal calls, simply leave out\n"
"`:\"phone-internal\"=>\"\"` out of the setting. The setting itself is in a\n"
"form of an array ( `{}` ).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:587
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ui_ticket_add_article_hint')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:591
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Show Email Address of Customer on Customer Selection (Ticket Creation)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:595
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, Zammad will not display the email addresses of customers.  The "
"below option allows you to change this behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:596
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_user_organization_selector_with_email', true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:601 src/en/reference/console.md:621
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current state of this setting with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:602
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ui_user_organization_selector_with_email')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:606
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change Font Settings for Outgoing HTML Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:608
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some clients (like Outlook) might fallback to other settings while it\n"
"might work for other clients.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:615
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The below setting allows you to adjust Zammad's email font setting. This "
"setting does not require a service restart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:616
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setting.set(\"html_email_css_font\", \"font-family:'Helvetica Neue', "
"Helvetica, Arial, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:622
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('html_email_css_font')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:626
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Highlight Customer's Open Ticket Count"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:630
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This option enhances the selected customer's open tickets count. It "
"highlights the count in different colors if they hit a threshold."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:631
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_sidebar_open_ticket_indicator_colored', true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:637
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Above settings has specific thresholds as follows. You **cannot** adjust "
"these thresholds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:642
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Situation / View      | no indication | warning (orange) | danger (red) "
"|\n"
"|-----------------------|---------------|------------------|--------------|\n"
"| **Ticket Zoom**       | \\< 2          | 2                | \\>= 3        "
"|\n"
"| **New Ticket dialog** | 0             | 1                | \\>= 2        "
"|\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:644
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate Attachment Tab in Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:648
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This option activates a new tab in the right sidebar in the ticket view "
"which shows all attachments of the currently viewed ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:649
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_ticket_zoom_sidebar_article_attachments', 'true')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:653
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Time Period for Showing Customer Profile on New Calls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:659
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad shows the customer profile dialog when a call of this customer is "
"incoming and there is an existing ticket of this customer in this time "
"period. The default time period is 30 days. If there is no ticket in this "
"period, the customer dialog is not shown automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:661
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set the time period to 90 days:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:661
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('cti_customer_last_activity', '90')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:665
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set Public \"Notes\" as SLA relevant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:671
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Normally, notes aren't SLA relevant. Use the following command to include "
"publicly-visible notes when tracking SLA compliance (internal notes *will "
"never* affect SLA calculations). Be aware that this setting will disable the "
"option to delete public notes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:672
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, customers are not notified when public notes are added to a\n"
"ticket. Set up a trigger if you wish to change this behavior.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:678
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enable SLA to count notes as communication:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:678
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket::Article::Type.find_by(name:'note').update!(communication: true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:682
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enable SLA to ignore notes as communication:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:682
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket::Article::Type.find_by(name:'note').update!(communication: false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:686
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other Useful Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:688
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fetch Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:692
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The below command will do a manual fetch of mail channels. This will also "
"show errors that might appear within that process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:693
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channel.fetch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:697
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reprocess Failed Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:702
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When Zammad fetches an email it cannot parse (e.g. due to a parser bug or a "
"malformed message), it will store the email in the database and warn in the "
"monitoring section about it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:706
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case of a malformed message (e.g. an invalid email address in one of the "
"header fields), you may need to manually edit the email before Zammad can "
"process it. To do so, follow the steps below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:707
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Export all Failed Emails to a Local Folder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:708
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:export_all`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:714
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can find the location of the exported email in the output of your "
"console.  Every time you perform an export of failed (unprocessable) emails, "
"it creates one folder containing all failed emails at the time of execution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:715
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Edit the Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:719
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The email has been exported in the step above. Now you can have a look at it "
"and try to repair it. Make sure to leave the file name untouched, as the "
"import will otherwise fail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:720
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import and Reprocess Locally Modified Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:723
#, markdown-text
msgid "After editing the email, run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:724
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:import path/to/your/email.eml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:732
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This will apply your changes from the file to the database. You can also "
"pass the entire folder as argument, so all `.eml` files in it will we "
"imported and reprocessed. If the reprocessing of the email was successful, "
"the file(s) will be deleted, and the empty folder removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:733
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Make sure to run these commands only from the main Zammad folder\n"
"`/opt/zammad`. There may be problems if you try to run it from within\n"
"the generated subfolder.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:739
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Delete Unwanted Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:743
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case of unwanted emails such as spam, you can delete them from the "
"database after exporting them with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:743
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:delete path/to/your/email.eml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:750
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you pass the export folder as argument instead, all contained emails will "
"be removed from the database, their files deleted and finally the empty "
"folder removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:751
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fill a Test System With Test Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:753
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Don't run this in a productive environment! This can slow down Zammad\n"
"and is hard to revert!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:762
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The below command will add `50` agents, `1000` customers, `20` groups, `40` "
"organizations, `5` new overviews and `100` tickets. You can always use `0` "
"to not create specific items. Zammad will create random data which make no "
"logical sense."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:763
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FillDb.load(agents: 50,customers: 1000,groups: 20,organizations: "
"40,overviews: 5,tickets: 100,)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:767
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deleting Records"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:769
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"☠️ The commands listed here cause **irrecoverable data loss**! Only\n"
"proceed if you know what you're doing and you\n"
"[have a backup](/en/tutorials/backup-restore)!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:775
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Removing Tickets (And Their Articles)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:778
#, markdown-text
msgid "Delete a ticket (specified by database ID):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:778
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.find(4).destroy\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:782
#, markdown-text
msgid "Delete all tickets:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:782
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:786
#, markdown-text
msgid "Keep some tickets (specified by database ID); delete the rest:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:786
#, no-wrap
msgid "tickets_to_keep = [1, 2, 3]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:789
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.where.not(id: tickets_to_keep).destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:793
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Removing Users"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:795
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Customers **may not** be deleted while they have tickets remaining in\n"
"the system.\n"
"\n"
"As such, the examples below will delete not only the specified\n"
"customers, but **all tickets associated with them**, as well. Below\n"
"commands delete without any further warnings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:805
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you're not sure what to do and need to learn more about what Zammad\n"
"does upon removing users, please consider using Zammad's UI options in\n"
"stead. You can find the data privacy feature in Zammad's admin interface "
"under\n"
"*System > Data Privacy*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:813
#, markdown-text
msgid "Removing users is possible in 2 ways: A single user and in bulk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:816
#, markdown-text
msgid "Remove a single user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:817
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(email: '<email address>').destroy\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:821
#, markdown-text
msgid "Remove several users:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:822
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"User.where(\n"
"      email: ['<email address 1>', '<email address 2>']\n"
"   ).destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:828
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Removing Organizations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:830
#, no-wrap
msgid "Removing an organization does **not** delete associated customers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:834
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Select organizations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:837
#, markdown-text
msgid "By \"active\" status:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:837
#, no-wrap
msgid "organizations = Organization.where(active: false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:842
#, markdown-text
msgid "By name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:842
#, no-wrap
msgid "organizations = Organization.where(name: 'Acme')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:847
#, markdown-text
msgid "By partial match on notes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:847
#, no-wrap
msgid "organizations = Organization.where('note LIKE ?', '%foo%')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:851
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Preview affected organizations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:852
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"puts organizations.map { |org| \"ORGANIZATION #{org.name}\" "
"}.join(\"\\n\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/console.md:856
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Proceed with Deletion"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:858
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"organizations.each do |org|\n"
"    puts %{Preparing deletion of organization \"#{org.name}\"...}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:862
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"org.members.each do |member|\n"
"    puts \"  Removing #{member.fullname} from organization...\"\n"
"    member.update!(organization_id: nil)\n"
"end\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:868
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    puts \"  Deleting #{org.name}...\"\n"
"    org.destroy\n"
"   end\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:874
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Removing System Records"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:877
#, markdown-text
msgid "Remove all online notifications:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:878
#, no-wrap
msgid "OnlineNotification.destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:883
#, markdown-text
msgid "Remove all entries from the Activity Stream (dashboard):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:884
#, no-wrap
msgid "ActivityStream.destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:889
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Remove entries for all recently viewed objects(tickets, users, "
"organizations):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:890
#, no-wrap
msgid "RecentView.destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:896
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Remove all history information from tickets, users and organizations "
"(dangerous!):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:897
#, no-wrap
msgid "History.destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:901
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reset Zammad Installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:903
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"Below commands are incomplete intentionally, error outputs will hint you\n"
"through! The following operations will cause data loss and are for\n"
"development / testing only.\n"
"\n"
"Don't forget to stop Zammad before trying to drop the database!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:912
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake db:drop\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:915
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake db:create\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:918
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake db:migrate\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:921
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake db:seed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:1 src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Docker Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Find the available docker environment variables below with default values, "
"if applicable. You might also be interested in the [environment variables "
"documentation](/en/reference/env-vars)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`VERSION` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"<current stable version of "
"Zammad>\"/>\n"
": Allows customization of the Zammad image tag. Example: `6.3.1-54`.\n"
"  This default version may be increased when you update your Zammad docker\n"
"  stack. Please see the example env template for more details on this "
"variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`AUTOWIZARD_JSON`\n"
": This variable allows you to provide initial configuration data for your\n"
"  instance. Autowizard JSON is out of scope of this documentation, however "
"this\n"
"  example file should help.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEB_CONCURRENCY`\n"
": Allows spawning `n` workers to allow more simultaneous connections for\n"
"  Zammad's  web UI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_SESSION_JOBS_CONCURRENT`\n"
": Allows spawning `n` session job workers to release pressure from "
"Zammad's\n"
"  background worker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_SCHEDULED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": Allows spawning `1` independent scheduled job worker to reduce pressure\n"
"  from Zammad's background worker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": Allows spawning n delayed job workers to reduce pressure from Zammad's\n"
"  background worker.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`RAILS_TRUSTED_PROXIES` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"['127.0.0.1', "
"'::1']\"/>\n"
": By default Zammad trusts localhost proxies only.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`MEMCACHE_SERVERS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-memcached:11211\"/>\n"
": Provide your own Memcached instance to Zammad if you already have one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`REDIS_URL` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"redis://zammad-redis:6379\"/>\n"
": Provide your own Redis instance if you already have one. Please note "
"that\n"
"this method currently does not allow authentication.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:49
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_ENABLED` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": Setting this variable to false will allow you to run your Zammad without\n"
"Elasticsearch. Please note that we strongly advise against doing so.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-elasticsearch\"/>\n"
": Provide a host name or address to your external Elasticsearch cluster.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:60
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"9200\"/>\n"
": Provide a different port for Elasticsearch if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:63
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_SCHEMA` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"http\"/>\n"
": By default, Elasticsearch is reachable via HTTP.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_NAMESPACE` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad\"/>\n"
": With this name space all Zammad related indexes will be created. Change "
"this\n"
"  if you're using external clusters.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_REINDEX` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": By default the docker-compose will always re-index upon a restart. On "
"big\n"
"  installations, this may be troublesome.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:71
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Disabling this setting requires you to re-index your search index "
"manually\n"
"  whenever you upgrade to a new Zammad version!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_SSL_VERIFY` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": Allows you to let the compose scripts ignore self signed SSL "
"certificates\n"
"  for your Elasticsearch installation if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:84
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-postgresql\"/>\n"
": Host name of your PostgreSQL server. Use your own if you already have "
"one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"5432\"/>\n"
": Adjust the Port of your PostgreSQL server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:90
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_USER` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad\"/>\n"
": The database user for Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:93
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_PASS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad\"/>\n"
": The password of Zammads database user.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_DB` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad_production\"/>\n"
": Zammads database to use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_OPTIONS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"?pool=50\"/>\n"
": Additional postgresql parameters to be appended to the database URI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:102
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_DB_CREATE` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"true\"/>\n"
": By default Zammad creates the required database.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "  On dedicated database servers, this setting might be troublesome.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:112
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_EXPOSE_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"8080\"/>\n"
": The port to be exposed for accessing the Zammad stack from "
"outside. Change\n"
"  this to another value if you already have an existing service listening "
"on\n"
"  this port.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:115
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"8080\"/>\n"
": The internal port the nginx service will listen on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:119
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_SERVER_NAME` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"_\"/>\n"
": By default the Nginx container of Zammad will respond to all "
"request. You\n"
"  can provide your IP / FQDN if you want to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:124
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_SERVER_SCHEME` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"\\$scheme\"/>\n"
": If the Nginx container for Zammad is not the upstream server (means if "
"you\n"
"  are using another proxy in front of nginx) you might want to change "
"this.\n"
"  You can set the correct scheme `http` or `https` if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:127
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILSSERVER_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" "
"text=\"zammad-railsserver\"/>\n"
": Host name of the rails server container.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:130
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILSSERVER_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"3000\"/>\n"
": Port of Zammads rails server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:133
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEBSOCKET_HOST` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"zammad-websocket\"/>\n"
": Host name of Zammads websocket server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-env-vars.md:135
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEBSOCKET_PORT` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"6042\"/>\n"
": Port of Zammad's websocket server.\n"
msgstr ""

