#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can find a comprehensive list of all default object attributes indexed "
"by Elasticsearch below. In other words, if you wish to find a ticket, "
"article, or user via the Zammad search box, Elasticsearch can match on any "
"(or all) of the fields below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"- <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"SLA\"/>: Attributes marked as SLA are only set "
"if\n"
"  the ticket is affected by SLA calculation. Please note that some "
"attributes\n"
"  may not be set if specific conditions are not met.\n"
"- Also note that some attributes may be reset to `null` if no longer "
"applicable.\n"
"- `note` attribute: Note attributes usually are empty if not specified via "
"console or API.\n"
"- Timestamps: All timestamps provided by Zammad are UTC by default. This "
"also\n"
"  applies to times provided by Elasticsearch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
