#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "Zammad supports three different authentication methods for its API."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP Basic Authentication (username/password)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The username / password must be provided as HTTP header in the HTTP call.  "
"This authentication method can be disabled and may not be available in your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ curl -u {username}:{password} https://{fqdn}/{endpoint}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We strongly suggest against using basic authentication. Use access\n"
"tokens when ever possible!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP Token Authentication (access token)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The access token must be provided as HTTP header in the HTTP call.  Each "
"user can create several access tokens in their user preferences.  This "
"authentication method can be disabled and may not be available in your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ curl -H \"Authorization: Token token={your_token}\" "
"https://{fqdn}/{endpoint}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "OAuth2 (token access)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The token must be provided as HTTP header in your calls.  This allows 3rd "
"party applications to authenticate against Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer {your_token}\" https://{fqdn}/{endpoint}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:70
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints and Example Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:77
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For simplicity we'll not provide specific commands on the next pages, but "
"instead tell the possible call method (e.g. `GET`) and the endpoint to use "
"(e.g. `/api/v1/users`). In case Zammad expects information within these "
"endpoint urls, we'll put them into curly braces like so: "
"`/api/v1/users/{user id}`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:81
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The response format will be a complete JSON response from a default Zammad "
"instance. Please keep in mind that you may see more fields or general "
"information in case you added objects or other information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:82
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Content Type"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad returns JSON payloads whenever you retrieve data. If you're going to "
"provide data, no matter of the general request type, don't forget to provide "
"the content type `application/json` as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Response Payloads (Expand)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad always returns information including hints to all relations. If you "
"need more information than that (because IDs may not be enough) you can also "
"extend your endpoint calls with `?expand=true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:97
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This switch will provide even more information - at least named relations on "
"top of the ID ones. Below you can find two examples, one for ticket and one "
"for user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details|tabs)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== User payload\n"
"\n"
"<<< @/fixtures/rest-api/users/get-id-res.json\n"
"\n"
"=== Ticket payload\n"
"\n"
"<<< @/fixtures/rest-api/tickets/get-id-res.json\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that Core Workflows may restrict access to attributes or\n"
"values.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:117
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pagination"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:121
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"As Zammad limits the number of returned objects for performance reasons, you "
"may have to use pagination at some points."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Number of returned objects:** Zammad has hard limits for the\n"
"maximum returned objects. You can't raise these limits.\n"
"\n"
"**Number of total to return objects:** Zammad does not provide a\n"
"total count of objects available for your query. This forces you to\n"
"cycle through the pages until Zammad no longer returns further\n"
"objects.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In order to use pagination you'll need two get options: `per_page` and "
"`page`. Combine them to receive 5 results from the first result page: "
"`?page=1&per_page=5` - increase page count to get more results."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:136
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sorting Search Results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:139
#, markdown-text
msgid "Zammad allows you to sort your search results by field if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:140
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`sort_by`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:143
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Append `?sort_by={row name}` to your query to sort by a specific row that "
"appears in the search result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:144
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`order_by`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:147
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Append `?order_by={direction}` to your query to switch in between ascending "
"and descending order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:149
#, markdown-text
msgid "Directions are: `asc` and `desc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Usually you'll want to combine both parameters in your searches -\n"
"e.g.: `?query={search string}&sort_by={row name}&order_by={direction}`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:155
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Actions On Behalf of Other Users"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:159
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Requirement:** the user used for running the query on behalf requires\n"
"`admin.user` permission.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:162
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Running API queries on behalf of other users allows you to e.g. create "
"tickets by a different user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:165
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To do so, add a new HTTP header named `From` to your request. The value of "
"this header can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:169
#, markdown-text
msgid "user ID"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:169
#, markdown-text
msgid "user login"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:169
#, markdown-text
msgid "user email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:171
#, markdown-text
msgid "`From` is available for all endpoints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:172
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:177
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The API expects UTF-8 encoding. Keep in mind that especially when using URLs "
"with get options (e.g. `?query=this`) you may need to encode your URL "
"accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:180
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to learn more about URL encoding, [this Wikipedia "
"article](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding) may be of help"
msgstr ""

