#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:58
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optional Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We collected some useful settings you may want to apply. For further "
"information please have a look at [Elastic's "
"documentation](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/index.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:64
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Index Namespacing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Useful when connecting multiple services or Zammad instances to a single "
"Elasticsearch server (to prevent name collisions during indexing)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_index', Socket.gethostname.downcase + "
"'_zammad')\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:72
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "File-Attachment Indexing Rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:77
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad supports searching in file attachments, which means Elasticsearch has "
"to index those, too. Limiting such indexing can help preserve system "
"resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid "Files with these extensions will not be indexed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_ignore',\\\n"
"[ '.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg', '.mpeg', '.mpg', '.mov', '.bin', '.exe', '.box', "
"'.mbox' ] )\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid "Files larger than this size (in MB) will not be indexed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "zammad run rails r \"Setting.set('es_attachment_max_size_in_mb', 50)\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Troubleshooting unsuccessful or issue not described?\n"
"\n"
"If you can't solve your issue using the provided troubleshooting steps\n"
"or can't find your particular issue described here, feel free to [ask\n"
"the community](https://community.zammad.org) for technical assistance.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:100
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Data Missing From the Web-UI / Search Data Missing or Incomplete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A commonly reported issue is data missing from the Web-UI. This could be "
"tickets, articles, users or anything else [indexed by "
"Elasticsearch](/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes)  and can be caused by "
"missing or incomplete indexes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:110
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are experiencing this issue and installed Elasticsearch according to "
"our [installation guide](/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch), please follow "
"these steps to make sure Elasticsearch is working correctly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:111
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Verify Elasticsearch is Running"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl status elasticsearch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:119
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This should output something like the following, make sure it says `Active: "
"active (running)`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"● elasticsearch.service - Elasticsearch\n"
"   Loaded: loaded (/lib/systemd/system/elasticsearch.service; enabled; "
"vendor preset: enabled)\n"
"   Active: active (running) since Tue 2021-07-20 09:38:21 UTC; 1h 4min ago\n"
"   Docs: https://www.elastic.co\n"
"   Main PID: 1790 (java)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:129
#, markdown-text
msgid "Otherwise, try restarting it and check again:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:130
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl restart elasticsearch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch.md:134
#, no-wrap
