msgid "`<domain>`: Windows domain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:122
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<master-domain-controller>`: Master domain controller IP/FQD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:124
#, markdown-text
msgid "The commands below will prompt for the users password:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "setspn -s HTTP/<zammad-host> <service-acct>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ktpass /princ HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN> \\\n"
"        /mapuser <service-acct> \\\n"
"        /crypto AES256-SHA1 \\\n"
"        /ptype KRB5_NT_PRINCIPAL \\\n"
"        /pass <password> -SetPass +DumpSalt \\\n"
"        /target <master-domain-controller> \\\n"
"        /out zammad.keytab\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:138
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1d. Note the secret key and version number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:142
#, markdown-text
msgid "The output of the command above contains important data for Step 2e below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:143
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using legacy password setting method\n"
"Failed to set property 'servicePrincipalName' to 'HTTP/<zammad-host>' on Dn "
"'CN=Zammad Service,DC=<domain>,DC=<tld>': 0x13.\n"
"WARNING: Unable to set SPN mapping data.\n"
"If <service-acct> already has an SPN mapping installed for "
"HTTP/<zammad-host>, this is no cause for concern.\n"
"Building salt with principalname HTTP/<zammad-host> and domain <domain> "
"(encryption type 18)...\n"
"Hashing password with salt \"<domain><service-acct>\".\n"
"Key created.\n"
"Output keytab to zammad.keytab:\n"
"Keytab version: 0x502\n"
"keysize 67 <service-acct>@<domain> ptype 1 (KRB5_NT_PRINCIPAL) vno 3 etype "
"0x12 (AES256-SHA1) keylength 32 "
"(0x5ee827c30c736dd4095c9cbe146eabc216415b1ddb134db6aabd61be8fdf7fb1) // "
"[!code focus]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:157
#, markdown-text
msgid "On the last line, take note of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:160
#, markdown-text
msgid "the secret key in parentheses at the end (**0x5ee827...**)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:160
#, markdown-text
msgid "the secret key version number preceded by `vno` (**3**)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:161
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Remove NGINX, Set up Apache + Kerberos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:165
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Next, the Zammad host must be configured to support Kerberos (and to accept "
"auth credentials provided by the Active Directory server)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:169
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In most cases, you would have to recompile NGINX from source with an extra "
"module to enable Kerberos support. To get around this, we will use Apache, "
"which offers Kerberos support through a plug-in module instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "All commands in this section must be run as root (or with `sudo`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:174
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2a. Turn Off NGINX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:176
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This will take your Zammad instance **offline** until Apache is fully\n"
"configured and running.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:182
#, markdown-text
msgid "Turn off nginx:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl stop nginx\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:186
#, markdown-text
msgid "Keep it off after reboot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ systemctl disable nginx\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:193
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you wish to minimize downtime, you can save this step for last; just bear "
"in mind that Apache will not start if the port it wants to listen on is "
"being used by NGINX."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:196
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If for any reason you can't complete this tutorial, simply turn off Apache "
"and restore NGINX:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:197
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```sh\n"
"systemctl stop apache2\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"systemctl disable apache2\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"systemctl enable nginx\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"systemctl start nginx\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:212
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2b. Pre-Configure Apache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:217
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This documentation expects a already working Apache configuration.  You "
"should have a look at the [webserver configuration "
"guide](/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md) before continuing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:218
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2c. Install Further Apache Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:220
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian & Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt update\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"apt install krb5-user libapache2-mod-auth-gssapi\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"yum install krb5-workstation mod_auth_kerb\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"zypper ref\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"zypper install krb5-client apache2-mod_auth_kerb\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:248
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2d. Enable Apache Modules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:252
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"SSO requires modules that are not enabled by default. By default you can use "
"`a2enmod` to do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:254
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== a2enmod (Debian & Ubuntu)\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"a2enmod auth_gssapi rewrite\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"systemctl restart apache2\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== a2enmod (OpenSUSE)\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"a2enmod auth_kerb rewrite\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"systemctl restart apache2\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== via configuration file (CentOS)\n"
"\n"
"add/uncomment the appropriate `LoadModule` statements in your Apache\n"
"config:\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"# /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf\n"
"\n"
"LoadModule auth_kerb_module /usr/lib/apache2/modules/mod_auth_kerb.so\n"
"LoadModule rewrite_module modules/mod_rewrite.so\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:288
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2e. Configure Kerberos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:292
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Kerberos realm configuration is how you tell the Zammad server how to reach "
"the *domain controller* (Active Directory server)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:294
#, markdown-text
msgid "Replace the following placeholders in the sample config below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:299
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<domain-controller>`: Domain controller IP/FQDN(s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:299
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<master-domain-controller>`: Master domain controller IP/FQDN (must not be "
"read-only, but can be the same as `<domain-controller>`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:300
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# /etc/krb5.conf\n"
"\n"
"[libdefaults]\n"
"   default_realm = <DOMAIN>\n"
"\n"
"   default_tkt_enctypes = aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96\n"
"   default_tgs_enctypes = aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96\n"
"   permitted_enctypes = aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96\n"
"\n"
"   kdc_timesync = 1\n"
"   ccache_type = 4\n"
"   forwardable = false\n"
"   proxiable = false\n"
"   fcc-mit-ticketflags = false\n"
"\n"
"[realms]\n"
"         # multiple KDCs ok (one `kdc = ...` definition per line)\n"
"         <DOMAIN> = {\n"
"                  kdc = <domain-controller>\n"
"                  admin_server = <master-domain-controller>\n"
"                  default_domain = <domain>\n"
"\n"
"                  # below is only for GSSAPI\n"
"                  auth_to_local = "
"RULE:[1:$1@$0](.*@<domain>)s/@<domain>$//\n"
"                  auth_to_local = DEFAULT\n"
"         }\n"
"\n"
"[domain_realm]\n"
"         .<domain> = <DOMAIN>\n"
"         <domain> = <DOMAIN>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:333
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2f. Generate Keytab"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:337
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Apache needs a Kerberos *keytab* (key table) to manage its shared secrets "
"with the domain controller."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:344
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<secret-key>`: Secret key (**omit the leading** `0x`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:344
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<vno>`: Secret key version number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:347
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The secret key and version number were found in `sso-register-spn` (Step 1d)  "
"above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:349
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter ktutil:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "ktutil\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:353
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add keytab:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:353
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ktutil: addent -key -p HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN> -k <vno> -e aes256-cts\n"
"Key for HTTP/<zammad-host>@<domain> (hex): <secret-key>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:358
#, markdown-text
msgid "Confirm the entry was added successfully:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:358
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ktutil: list\n"
"slot KVNO Principal\n"
"---- ---- ---------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"   1    3 HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:365
#, markdown-text
msgid "Write keytab to disk:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:365
#, no-wrap
msgid "ktutil: wkt /root/zammad.keytab\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:369
#, markdown-text
msgid "Leave ktutil:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:369
#, no-wrap
msgid "ktutil: quit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:375
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Then, place the keytab in the Apache config directory and set the "
"appropriate permissions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:376
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian, Ubuntu, OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"mv /root/zammad.keytab /etc/apache2/\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"chown root:www-data /etc/apache2/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"chmod 640 /etc/apache2/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"mv /root/zammad.keytab /etc/httpd/\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"chown root:apache /etc/httpd/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
"```sh\n"
"chmod 640 /etc/httpd/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:403
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2g. Configure Apache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:407
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Add the following directive to the end of the virtual host configuration "
"file to create your Kerberos SSO endpoint at `/auth/sso`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:409
#, markdown-text
msgid "Replace the following placeholders in the command below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:414
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian & Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"``` apache\n"
"# /etc/apache2/sites-available/zammad.conf\n"
"\n"
"<LocationMatch \"/auth/sso\">\n"
"   SSLRequireSSL\n"
"   AuthType GSSAPI\n"
"   AuthName \"Your Zammad\"\n"
"   GssapiBasicAuth On\n"
"   GssapiCredStore keytab:/etc/apache2/zammad.keytab\n"
"   GssapiLocalName On\n"
"   require valid-user\n"
"\n"
"   RewriteEngine On\n"
"   RewriteCond %{LA-U:REMOTE_USER} (.+)\n"
"   RewriteRule . - [E=RU:%1,NS]\n"
"   RequestHeader set X-Forwarded-User \"%{RU}e\" env=RU\n"
"</LocationMatch>\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS & OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"The configuration for CentOS and OpenSUSE below contains two\n"
"`Krb5KeyTab` lines! Keep only the one you need.\n"
"\n"
"``` apache\n"
"# /etc/apache2/sites-available/zammad.conf\n"
"\n"
"<LocationMatch \"/auth/sso\">\n"
"   SSLRequireSSL\n"
"   AuthType Kerberos\n"
"   AuthName \"Your Zammad\"\n"
"   KrbMethodNegotiate On\n"
"   KrbVerifyKDC On\n"
"   KrbMethodK5Passwd On\n"
"   KrbAuthRealms <DOMAIN>\n"
"   KrbLocalUserMapping on                 # strips @REALM suffix from "
"REMOTE_USER variable\n"
"   KrbServiceName HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN>\n"
"   Krb5KeyTab /etc/apache2/zammad.keytab  # Ubuntu, Debian, & openSUSE\n"
"   Krb5KeyTab /etc/httpd/zammad.keytab    # CentOS\n"
"   require valid-user\n"
"\n"
"   RewriteEngine On\n"
"   RewriteCond %{LA-U:REMOTE_USER} (.+)\n"
"   RewriteRule . - [E=RU:%1,NS]\n"
"   RequestHeader set X-Forwarded-User \"%{RU}e\" env=RU\n"
"</LocationMatch>\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:467
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2g. Restart Apache to Apply Changes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:469
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:167
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl restart apache2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:473
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Enable SSO in Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:477
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, enable \"Authentication via SSO\" in Zammad's Admin Panel under\n"
"*Settings > Security > Third-Party Applications*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:481
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> [!NOTE]\n"
"> On older versions of Zammad, visit `https://your.zammad.host/auth/sso`\n"
"> to sign in.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:482
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Configure Client System (Windows Only)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:486
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For the full SSO experience (i.e. for passwordless one-click sign-in), "
"Zammad users must:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:490
#, markdown-text
msgid "be on the Active Directory server's local intranet; and"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:490
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"modify their network settings for the Zammad host to be treated as a local "
"intranet server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:493
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Without this step, users must enter their Active Directory credentials "
"during SSO."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== IE / Edge / Chromium\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This setting can be centrally managed across the entire intranet using\n"
"a **group policy object** (GPO).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"1. Add your Zammad FQDN in Internet Options under *Security > Local\n"
"   Intranet > Sites > Advanced*.\n"
"2. Select \"Require server verification (https:) for all sites in this\n"
"   zone\".\n"
"3. Under *Security level for this zone > Custom level... > Settings\n"
"   \\> User Authentication > Logon*, select \"Automatic logon only in\n"
"   Intranet Zone\".\n"
"\n"
"=== Firefox\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|info)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This option cannot be centrally managed because it is set in the\n"
"browser rather than Windows Settings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"1.  Enter `about:config` in the address bar. Click **Accept the risk and\n"
"    continue**.\n"
"2.  Search for the `network.negotiate-auth.trusted-uris` option.\n"
"3.  Double-click to edit, then add your Zammad FQDN.\n"
"4.  Restart Firefox to apply your changes.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:533
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Are all relevant FQDNs/hostnames reachable from your Active Directory and "
"Zammad servers (including each other's)?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:533
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Are the system clocks of your Active Directory and Zammad servers "
"synchronized within five minutes of each other? Kerberos is a time-sensitive "
"protocol!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:534
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Errors in Apache Logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:536
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Try raising your Apache log level temporarily.**\n"
"\n"
"Add `LogLevel debug` to your virtual host configuration, then restart\n"
"the service to apply the changes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:543
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An unsupported mechanism was requested"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:546
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Does your Active Directory service account have **Kerberos AES 256-bit "
"encryption** enabled?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:550
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If for some reason your server does not support AES 256-bit encryption, the "
"LDAP Wiki has [more information about Kerberos encryption "
"types](https://ldapwiki.com/wiki/MsDS-SupportedEncryptionTypes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:551
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Failed to verify krb5 credentials: Key version is not available"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:554
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Did you use the exact **version number** (`vno`) provided by `ktpass`\n"
"when `generating your keytab <sso-generate-keytab>`?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:556 src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:562
#, markdown-text
msgid "Try generating it again, just to be sure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:557
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
